WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.385 --> 00:00:01.749
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.749 --> 00:00:06.477
- [Narrator] This is Kizzy, a
black and white ruffed lemur.

00:00:06.477 --> 00:00:10.082
She calls the rainforests
of eastern Madagascar home,

00:00:10.082 --> 00:00:13.415
and unfortunately, home is disappearing.

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:17.119
Black and white ruffed
lemurs grow up to four feet

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:19.569
and close to 10 pounds,

00:00:19.569 --> 00:00:23.993
making them one of the
larger lemur species.

00:00:23.993 --> 00:00:25.881
Besides making for a curious look,

00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:30.170
their extra thick fur helps
protect them from rainfall,

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.337
as water just runs off it.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.657
They are an all female
dominant social group

00:00:35.657 --> 00:00:37.745
and live mostly high in the trees

00:00:37.745 --> 00:00:40.662
where they search for fruit to eat.

00:00:41.906 --> 00:00:44.513
While they don't have
many natural predators,

00:00:44.513 --> 00:00:47.359
accelerated habitat loss from logging

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:50.359
has left them critically endangered.

00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:54.789
This is the black and white ruffed lemur.

